---
/**
 * GTM's `<noscript>` fallback, kept as supplied in the owner's install snippet (2026-09-05).
 *
 * It belongs immediately after `<body>`, which is why it is a separate component from
 * `Analytics.astro` (that one lives in `<head>`).
 *
 * **Known limitation, recorded rather than hidden:** unlike the head tag, this CANNOT be host-gated,
 * because gating is done in JavaScript and this element exists precisely for agents that run none.
 * So it is the one analytics surface that is not inert on preview/`*.workers.dev` URLs before
 * cutover. The exposure is small — it fires only for a visitor that executes no JavaScript *and*
 * loads iframes, which excludes ordinary browsers and most crawlers — and GA4 cannot record a
 * session from it either way. Noted in `docs/DECISIONS.md` §12a.
 */
import { GTM_ID } from "../lib/analytics";
---

<noscript>
	<iframe
		src={`https://www.googletagmanager.com/ns.html?id=${GTM_ID}`}
		height="0"
		width="0"
		style="display:none;visibility:hidden"
		title="Google Tag Manager"></iframe>
</noscript>
